f 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287656 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186287102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287656 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186287126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287656 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287656 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287656 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186286124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287656 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb288b6a-0ce0-5325-bbb2-0ee9ec1811d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181689" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/32/32168a2cb1fe14dbc88725347611ae5951198e81dfaa0b41e780106750bbb741.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,3x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,\\frac{x}{4}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "281f8e94-72c2-5b73-8bcb-5cb4814a0f37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287725 #edb/ref 1074 "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=3x$ and *below* the line $y=\\frac{x}{4}.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>3x,\\,y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3x<y<\\frac{x}{4}.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=3x$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\n3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3x\\le y<\\frac{x}{4}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/66/664c70223ca8a6219b04a287c779d20bf0f88d770920d1357303721574d90787.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,{x}^{2}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f80556dc-02e0-555b-8ef8-6bae1cda35bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287768 #edb/ref 1074 "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $y={x}^{2}$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge {x}^{2}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge {x}^{2}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182013" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/77/7703b8c621b268a9fcbb412cd3a0617045145d475024dc91cecfa09a18fc8712.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,-2\\}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49192157-aea0-5727-927f-dcfccbbb5607" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287790 #edb/ref 1074 "The points in our set include all those that lie *right* the line $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx>-2\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $x=-2$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge -2\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/98/980ae73286ed41ed0c6f074a4bed5b35fa852dd608fb0a1a561f26a7eac60ea7.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8779b713-2ad1-53d1-a3e6-394f41bc52c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287798 #edb/ref 1074 "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *to the left* the line $x=2.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx<2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\nx<2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,x<2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409894 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409894 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409894 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53607ff6-5913-50ea-923c-e269930ccd31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409895 #edb/ref 1080 "<" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409895 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409895 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d74e258e-f0dd-579c-9148-3c83bfa32b0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409896 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409896 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409896 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9099832-9536-5764-b8f9-82d9f50c96e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
